**Other Expressions for the Radial Functions (Valid Over More Limited Regions)**

**20.6.12**: \(Me_{2^{d}}^{(p)}(z,q)\!=\!\!\left[ee_{2^{d}}(0,q)\right]^{-1}\sum\limits_{k=0}^{n} \left(-1\right)^{k+r}\!\!A_{2k}^{2}(q)Z_{2k}^{i(p)}(2\sqrt{q}\,\,\cosh\,z)\)

\[Me_{4^{d}+1}^{(p)}(z,q)\!=\!\!\left[ee_{2^{d}+1}(0,q)\right]^{-1}\sum\limits_{k= 0}^{n}\left(-1\right)^{k+r}\!\!A_{2k}^{2r}\!\!+\!\!1(q)Z_{2k+1}^{(p)}(2\sqrt{q} \,\cosh\,z)\]
**20.6.13**: \(Me_{3^{d}}^{i(p)}(z,q)\!=\!\!\left[se_{2^{d}}^{\prime}(0,q)\right]^{-1}\tanh\,z \sum\limits_{k=1}^{n}\left(-1\right)^{k+r}\!\!2kB_{2k}^{2}(q)Z_{2k}^{i(p)}(2 \sqrt{q}\,\cosh\,z)\)

\[Me_{2^{d}+1}^{(p)}(z,q)\!=\!\!\left[se_{2^{d}+1}^{\prime}(0,q)\right]^{-1}\tanh \,z\sum\limits_{k=0}^{n}\left(-1\right)^{k+r}\!\!2kB_{2k+1}^{2r}(q)Z_{2k+1}^{( p)}(2\sqrt{q}\,\cosh\,z)\]

Valid for \(\mathscr{R}\!\!z\!\!>\!\!0\), \(\left|\cosh\,z\right|\!\!>\!\!1\); if \(j\!=\!1\), valid for all \(z\). They agree with 20.6.7-20.6.10 if the Bessel functions \(Y_{n}(2q^{d}\,\cosh\,z)\) are made single-valued in a suitable way. For example, let

\[Y_{n}(u)\!=\!\!\frac{2}{\pi}\left(\ln\,u\right)\!J_{n}(u)\!+\!\phi(u)\]

where \(\phi(u)\) is single-valued for all finite values of \(u\). With \(u\!=\!2q^{d}\,\cosh\,z\), define

**20.6.14**: \(\ln\,(2q^{d}\,\cosh\,z)\!\!=\!\!\ln\,2q^{d}\!+\!z\!\!+\!\!\ln\,\frac{1}{2}(1 \!+\!e^{-u})\!\!-\!\!\frac{\pi}{2}\!\leq\!\arg\,\,\lambda(1\!+\!e^{-u})\!\leq \!\!\frac{\pi}{2}\). (If \(q\) is not positive, the phase of \(\ln\,2q^{d}\) must also be specified, although this specification will not affect continuity with respect to \(z\). If \(Y_{n}(u)\) is defined from some other expression, the definition must be compatible with 20.6.14.)

